From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: count stations from the live provider snapshot

The AP Metrics report serialized station records from client_stats_map but
bounded that serialization with a count from associated_devices_map.  The
latter is event-backed history and can be empty when a station, especially a
gateway backhaul STA, associated before OneWifi started.  The live HAL/RBUS
provider still reports that station, but sta_cnt was forced to zero and the
existing EasyMesh metrics-seeding path never received it.

Use the live provider map as both the count and the data source.  This also
prevents an inactive historical association from inflating the allocation or
the advertised associated-station count.  The change is platform-independent:
an AP Metrics snapshot must describe the provider snapshot it serializes.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/apps/em/wifi_em.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -1928,8 +1928,13 @@ static int ap_report_push_cb(em_ap_report_callback_arg_t *args)
             //index cannot be vap index below right for cache retrieval, have to search in the all cache for each vaps and check vap index
             ap_metrics = &em_ap_metrics_report_cache.radio_report[radio_index].ap_data[cache_vap_index].ap_metrics;
-            ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas = hash_map_count(
-                wifi_mgr->radio_config[radio_index].vaps.rdk_vap_array[j].associated_devices_map);
-            vap_report->sta_cnt = ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas;
+            /* Serialize and count the same authoritative live snapshot.  The
+             * event-backed associated_devices_map can miss a station which
+             * associated before OneWifi started, while client_stats_map is
+             * refreshed by the current HAL provider response. */
+            vap_report->sta_cnt = hash_map_count(
+                em_ap_metrics_report_cache.radio_report[radio_index]
+                    .ap_data[cache_vap_index].client_stats_map);
+            ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas = vap_report->sta_cnt;
             memcpy(ap_metrics->bssid, vap_info->u.bss_info.bssid, sizeof(bssid_t));
             memcpy(&vap_report->vap_metrics, ap_metrics, sizeof(ap_metrics_t));
             to_mac_str(vap_info->u.bss_info.bssid, bss_str);
